WEBVTT

1
00:00:10.334 --> 00:00:14.450
Tom woke up first, and he wondered where he was.

2
00:00:14.451 --> 00:00:18.345
Then he remembered: he was a pirate on Jackson Island.

3
00:00:18.346 --> 00:00:22.101
The dawn was cool and gray, and there were dewdrops on the grass.

4
00:00:22.102 --> 00:00:26.839
Their campfire was almost out; only smoke rose from the ashes.

5
00:00:26.840 --> 00:00:33.181
Tom woke the other boys up, and they went for a swim in the river.

6
00:00:33.182 --> 00:00:39.187
They came back to camp happy and refreshed. They restarted the campfire.

7
00:00:39.188 --> 00:00:43.766
Joe made hickory tea, and Huck and Tom both caught some fish.

8
00:00:43.767 --> 00:00:50.400
After a delicious fish fry breakfast, Tom said, "Let's really find that buried treasure!"

9
00:00:50.401 --> 00:00:52.768
Huck and Joe were eager to follow.

10
00:00:52.769 --> 00:00:58.956
They looked in less obvious places—inside hollow logs and under the roots of old trees.

11
00:00:58.957 --> 00:01:02.518
Soon the boys were hot, so they took another swim.

12
00:01:02.519 --> 00:01:07.826
Although they hadn't found any treasure, the boys were too happy to care.

13
00:01:07.827 --> 00:01:11.007
Even without a treasure, the boys felt rich.

14
00:01:11.008 --> 00:01:15.833
The island seemed like a large kingdom to them.

15
00:01:15.834 --> 00:01:22.171
However, after a second failed treasure hunt, the boys began to feel a kind of homesickness growing inside them.

16
00:01:22.172 --> 00:01:27.488
Tom and Joe missed their families, and all three missed their friends.

17
00:01:27.489 --> 00:01:32.193
During lunch the boys heard a loud noise coming from up the river.

18
00:01:32.194 --> 00:01:34.575
"What's that?" asked Joe.

19
00:01:34.576 --> 00:01:36.746
"Can't be thunder," said Huck.

20
00:01:36.747 --> 00:01:40.692
"Shh!" said Tom. "Listen."

21
00:01:40.693 --> 00:01:44.914
The boys listened, and soon they heard another boom!

22
00:01:44.915 --> 00:01:49.799
"Let's see what's making that noise," said Tom.

23
00:01:49.800 --> 00:01:53.930
The boys watched a ferry chugging its way slowly down the river.

24
00:01:53.931 --> 00:02:00.456
First, they saw a burst of black smoke from the ferry's deck, and then they heard boom again!

25
00:02:00.457 --> 00:02:05.695
"I know!" shouted Tom. "Somebody's drowned."

26
00:02:05.696 --> 00:02:11.583
"Yes," said Huck. "They did this last summer when Bill Turner drowned.

27
00:02:11.584 --> 00:02:15.306
They're shooting cannonballs into the water to make the body come up."

28
00:02:15.307 --> 00:02:20.128
"Really?" said Joe. "I wonder who's drowned."

29
00:02:20.129 --> 00:02:22.682
The boys continued to watch and listen.

30
00:02:22.683 --> 00:02:28.076
Then Tom said suddenly, "I know who's drowned! It's us!"

31
00:02:28.077 --> 00:02:31.025
"You're right," agreed Huck.

32
00:02:31.026 --> 00:02:34.528
"We're heroes," said Joe.

33
00:02:34.529 --> 00:02:37.917
The boys were pleased because they knew they were missed.

34
00:02:37.918 --> 00:02:40.892
They also knew that they must be the talk of the town.

35
00:02:40.893 --> 00:02:43.730
Being a pirate was wonderful.

36
00:02:43.731 --> 00:02:47.354
By evening the ferry had stopped searching.

37
00:02:47.355 --> 00:02:52.661
The boys ate supper around the campfire, and they tried to guess what people were saying about them.

38
00:02:52.662 --> 00:02:56.845
Tom thought about Aunt Polly and Joe thought about his mother.

39
00:02:56.846 --> 00:03:01.349
"Maybe it's time to go back," said Joe softly.

40
00:03:01.350 --> 00:03:07.921
Although Tom and Huck were thinking the same thing, they both said they didn't want to go home.

41
00:03:07.922 --> 00:03:12.321
Tom couldn't sleep. He decided to leave his aunt a message.

42
00:03:12.322 --> 00:03:18.421
He wrote a note on a piece of bark, and then rowed the raft down the river and back into town.

43
00:03:18.422 --> 00:03:22.444
When he got to his house, he saw that the lights were still on.

44
00:03:22.445 --> 00:03:25.117
Aunt Polly was talking to Joe's mother.

45
00:03:25.118 --> 00:03:30.313
Tom sneaked into the house and hid under a bed.

46
00:03:30.314 --> 00:03:33.862
From under the bed, Tom could see and hear everything.

47
00:03:33.863 --> 00:03:37.371
"What's making the candle flicker?" asked Aunt Polly.

48
00:03:37.372 --> 00:03:40.201
She looked and saw the door was open.

49
00:03:40.202 --> 00:03:44.215
"Strange things are happening here," said Joe's mother.

50
00:03:44.216 --> 00:03:47.878
Tom could see that her eyes were red, and she had been crying.

51
00:03:47.879 --> 00:03:54.031
"Well, our boys are better off in heaven than here," said Aunt Polly.

52
00:03:54.032 --> 00:03:57.204
Aunt Polly cried, and Tom felt awful.

53
00:03:57.205 --> 00:04:01.115
"My Joe was a good boy," said Joe's mother.

54
00:04:01.116 --> 00:04:05.571
"He was always up to mischief, but he had a good heart."

55
00:04:05.572 --> 00:04:11.897
Aunt Polly nodded, and she said between her cries, "My Tom was the same.

56
00:04:11.898 --> 00:04:14.818
I've been too strict with him recently.

57
00:04:14.819 --> 00:04:20.648
I even gave him medicine that wasn't fit for a cat."

58
00:04:20.649 --> 00:04:26.336
Joe's mother then shook her head and said, "I haven't been nice to Joe either.

59
00:04:26.337 --> 00:04:32.852
I punished him for drinking cream that I had thrown out because it was sour!

60
00:04:32.853 --> 00:04:37.086
Now I'll never see him again."

61
00:04:37.087 --> 00:04:40.876
"They must have drowned," Aunt Polly said tearfully.

62
00:04:40.877 --> 00:04:46.832
"If they don't turn up by tomorrow, the pastor says we'll hold funerals for them on Sunday."

63
00:04:46.833 --> 00:04:49.003
The two women cried.

64
00:04:49.004 --> 00:04:54.768
Tom almost cried too, but what his aunt had just said made him think.

65
00:04:54.769 --> 00:04:59.466
Soon the crying stopped, and Joe's mother said good-night and left.

66
00:04:59.467 --> 00:05:02.256
Aunt Polly knelt beside her bed and prayed.

67
00:05:02.257 --> 00:05:05.487
Her prayers were full of kind words for her nephew.

68
00:05:05.488 --> 00:05:09.469
When Aunt Polly fell asleep, Tom looked at his aunt for awhile.

69
00:05:09.470 --> 00:05:12.821
Then he bent down and kissed her on her cheek.

70
00:05:12.822 --> 00:05:16.658
Tom didn't leave the note because now he had a better idea.

71
00:05:16.659 --> 00:05:19.128
He rowed back to the island.

72
00:05:19.129 --> 00:05:24.088
When he arrived, he woke his fellow pirates and told them about his adventure.

73
00:05:24.089 --> 00:05:29.674
Joe asked lots of questions about his mother, and Tom patiently told his friends everything.

74
00:05:29.675 --> 00:05:35.046
But he kept his newest plan to himself.
